<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Fort Garry</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper Fort Garry was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> post built in the 1830s at the junction of the Red and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assiniboine">Assiniboine</a> rivers, in present-day Winnipeg. It was the administrative centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a>, and in November 1869 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> seized it and made it the seat of their provisional government. Only its stone gate survives today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-fort-garry.jpg" alt="Upper Fort Garry" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mortimer &amp; Co. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Fort_Garry_-_Winnipeg,_Manitoba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
